1
00:00:00,834 --> 00:00:02,836
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:11,052 --> 00:00:12,929
[Jepoy] <i>Julio Ardiente's in the hospital.</i>

3
00:00:13,012 --> 00:00:14,055
<i>He had a heart attack.</i>

4
00:00:14,139 --> 00:00:16,016
<i>Well, doctors found something different.</i>

5
00:00:16,099 --> 00:00:17,267
<i>Grandpa was strangled.</i>

6
00:00:17,350 --> 00:00:18,601
<i>That's outrageous.</i>

7
00:00:18,685 --> 00:00:20,895
<i>Your dad would never do that</i>
<i>to your grandfather.</i>

8
00:00:20,979 --> 00:00:22,689
[Diego] <i>What do you want from my family?</i>

9
00:00:22,772 --> 00:00:25,275
<i>Ever since you arrived,</i>
<i>bad things started happening.</i>

10
00:00:25,358 --> 00:00:26,192
[Ivy] <i>Stop the car.</i>

11
00:00:26,276 --> 00:00:27,569
[Diego] <i>Even if you won't</i>
<i>answer my question,</i>

12
00:00:27,652 --> 00:00:30,363
<i>I'll find out</i>
<i>who you really are, Miss Aguas.</i>

13
00:00:30,447 --> 00:00:32,824
<i>You shouldn't get dragged</i>
<i>into this, Diego.</i>

14
00:00:32,907 --> 00:00:35,160
<i>But if you get in my way,</i>

15
00:00:35,243 --> 00:00:37,370
<i>I have no choice</i>
<i>but to deal with you, too.</i>

16
00:00:37,454 --> 00:00:38,705
[Raul] <i>Why did you cover up for me?</i>

17
00:00:38,788 --> 00:00:42,959
[Emilia] <i>I will keep everything</i>
<i>a secret, if you do what I want.</i>

18
00:00:43,042 --> 00:00:45,295
[Raul] <i>You know what, Emilia?</i>
<i>If you think you can keep me</i>

19
00:00:45,378 --> 00:00:47,797
<i>on a leash, then you're wrong.</i>

20
00:00:47,881 --> 00:00:50,091
[Emilia] <i>On the contrary,</i>
<i>I don't want you here.</i>

21
00:00:50,175 --> 00:00:51,885
<i>You can stay with your relatives,</i>

22
00:00:51,968 --> 00:00:52,719
<i>if you still have any.</i>

23
00:00:52,802 --> 00:00:54,763
[Raul] <i>Love, I'm back.</i>

24
00:00:54,846 --> 00:00:57,390
[Emilia] <i>I am now</i>
<i>the matriarch of this family.</i>

25
00:00:57,474 --> 00:00:58,641
<i>My time has come.</i>

26
00:00:58,725 --> 00:01:01,394
<i>Now that the king is gone,</i>
<i>I shall reign as queen.</i>

27
00:01:01,478 --> 00:01:03,730
<i>I will not push through with my investment</i>

28
00:01:03,813 --> 00:01:05,815
<i>if it will inconvenience the farmers.</i>

29
00:01:05,899 --> 00:01:07,484
<i>Why is this so personal to you?</i>

30
00:01:07,567 --> 00:01:08,943
<i>Is there something you want to reveal?</i>

31
00:01:09,027 --> 00:01:10,695
<i>Like skeletons in the closet?</i>

32
00:01:10,779 --> 00:01:12,572
[Raul] <i>They may have killed Camia,</i>

33
00:01:12,655 --> 00:01:14,282
<i>but I brought you back as Jasmin.</i>

34
00:01:14,365 --> 00:01:17,452
<i>We'll use that against</i>
<i>the Ardientes someday.</i>

35
00:01:17,535 --> 00:01:19,037
[Arnaldo] <i>You're running</i>
<i>for the Senate? But I'm the one</i>

36
00:01:19,120 --> 00:01:20,830
<i>Grandpa's been grooming</i>
<i>to someday take his place.</i>

37
00:01:20,914 --> 00:01:24,125
<i>Someday your time will come.</i>
<i>But now, it is my time.</i>

38
00:01:24,209 --> 00:01:25,794
[Belen] <i>You need to tell the truth.</i>

39
00:01:25,877 --> 00:01:29,464
<i>If Emilia finds out</i>
<i>you're keeping a woman here,</i>

40
00:01:29,547 --> 00:01:32,342
<i>she won't just have your head,</i>
<i>she'll have Jasmin's, too.</i>

41
00:01:36,971 --> 00:01:37,972
Excuse me, ma'am.

42
00:01:39,516 --> 00:01:41,059
[Emilia] Hmm. Can I see the back?

43
00:01:41,518 --> 00:01:42,685
Bring it there.

44
00:01:44,562 --> 00:01:45,730
Good morning, Madam Governor.

45
00:01:45,814 --> 00:01:46,689
My name is Lara.

46
00:01:46,773 --> 00:01:49,609
I'm a member of the staff
of Congressman Julio Ardiente.

47
00:01:49,692 --> 00:01:50,944
I will be your executive assistant

48
00:01:51,027 --> 00:01:52,654
while the Congressman is recovering.

49
00:01:53,154 --> 00:01:55,865
I have my own executive
assistant at my office.

50
00:01:56,366 --> 00:01:57,826
But this is different, Madam.

51
00:01:57,909 --> 00:01:59,160
Since Congressman is unavailable,

52
00:01:59,244 --> 00:02:02,539
you'll be attending events
and managing his projects.

53
00:02:02,622 --> 00:02:04,457
And as your E.A, I will be providing you

54
00:02:04,541 --> 00:02:06,167
with the timetables and schedules.

55
00:02:08,670 --> 00:02:09,712
Fine.

56
00:02:11,381 --> 00:02:12,966
Can you look for my husband?

57
00:02:15,969 --> 00:02:19,055
A queen can't show up
without her king now, can she?

58
00:02:20,140 --> 00:02:20,890
No, Governor.

59
00:02:20,974 --> 00:02:24,477
You seem skilled and efficient,
so you better do your job now.

60
00:02:25,562 --> 00:02:26,479
Go.

61
00:02:28,106 --> 00:02:29,107
I said go.

62
00:02:34,320 --> 00:02:36,030
[siren wailing]

63
00:02:37,448 --> 00:02:39,367
[siren wailing]

64
00:02:40,660 --> 00:02:42,036
[siren wailing]

65
00:02:45,456 --> 00:02:49,836
-[cop] Get out! Get out! Quick!
-[people clamoring]

66
00:02:50,587 --> 00:02:52,589
[cop] Move aside!

67
00:02:57,635 --> 00:02:58,928
-Hurry up!
-The cops are here. Move it!

68
00:02:59,012 --> 00:03:00,805
-Put them all here.
-Hurry up. The cops are here.

69
00:03:02,348 --> 00:03:04,809
Gregorio Orallo, you are under arrest

70
00:03:04,893 --> 00:03:08,396
for running a gambling den
in Poblacion Ardiente.

71
00:03:08,479 --> 00:03:10,315
You have the right to remain silent.

72
00:03:10,398 --> 00:03:13,151
Anything you say can
and will be used against you.

73
00:03:16,654 --> 00:03:18,573
[cop] Over there! Over there!

74
00:03:18,656 --> 00:03:22,535
<i>Orallo. How many times</i>
<i>do I have to ask you?</i>

75
00:03:23,161 --> 00:03:25,663
<i>All I need is just your cooperation.</i>

76
00:03:25,747 --> 00:03:26,831
<i>But Governor…</i>

77
00:03:27,540 --> 00:03:30,543
<i>I do everything you and Raul</i>
<i>tell me to do.</i>

78
00:03:31,252 --> 00:03:34,547
<i>I can't go to jail. What about my family?</i>

79
00:03:34,631 --> 00:03:37,050
<i>My daughter is still young, Madam.</i>

80
00:03:37,800 --> 00:03:39,594
[chuckles]

81
00:03:41,679 --> 00:03:43,598
<i>She really is.</i>

82
00:03:44,682 --> 00:03:47,685
<i>And she is just so cute.</i>

83
00:03:48,061 --> 00:03:49,812
<i>Madam Governor, I'm begging you.</i>

84
00:03:50,647 --> 00:03:52,315
<i>Sir, please help me.</i>

85
00:03:52,398 --> 00:03:55,735
<i>Orallo, if you still want</i>
<i>to see your daughter…</i>

86
00:03:56,819 --> 00:03:58,780
<i>then do as I say.</i>

87
00:03:59,113 --> 00:04:00,990
<i>So, will you take the fall for us…</i>

88
00:04:03,868 --> 00:04:06,621
<i>or should I blow</i>
<i>your daughter's brains out?</i>

89
00:04:11,167 --> 00:04:14,045
-Take him in.
-Watch your head. Move it.

90
00:04:23,263 --> 00:04:25,515
[reporter on TV]
<i>After Gregorio Orallo cleared</i>

91
00:04:25,598 --> 00:04:28,977
<i>the names of Gov. Emilia Ardiente-Torillo,</i>

92
00:04:29,060 --> 00:04:31,062
<i>her husband Raul Torillo,</i>

93
00:04:31,145 --> 00:04:34,524
<i>and Sen. Pablo Alcantara</i>
<i>from the gambling scandal,</i>

94
00:04:34,607 --> 00:04:36,734
<i>he admitted he was Poblacion Ardiente's</i>

95
00:04:36,818 --> 00:04:38,194
<i>resident gambling lord.</i>

96
00:04:38,278 --> 00:04:40,154
<i>He was later found dead in his cell</i>

97
00:04:40,238 --> 00:04:41,739
<i>in the evening after his arrest.</i>

98
00:04:41,823 --> 00:04:44,158
<i>According to the police,</i>
<i>there was no foul play,</i>

99
00:04:44,242 --> 00:04:45,368
<i>and Orallo committed suicide.</i>

100
00:04:45,451 --> 00:04:48,413
<i>Here is Gov. Ardiente-Torillo's statement.</i>

101
00:04:48,496 --> 00:04:50,790
[Emilia] <i>What happened today</i>
<i>was unfortunate.</i>

102
00:04:51,291 --> 00:04:53,584
<i>But if there's one good thing about this,</i>

103
00:04:53,668 --> 00:04:56,504
<i>it's that the gambling operations</i>

104
00:04:56,587 --> 00:04:58,423
<i>that continue to tarnish the name</i>

105
00:04:58,506 --> 00:05:02,176
<i>and image of Poblacion Ardiente,</i>
<i>has come to an end.</i>

106
00:05:03,052 --> 00:05:06,389
<i>As the governor and mother of our town,</i>

107
00:05:06,472 --> 00:05:12,812
<i>I promise to continue getting</i>
<i>rid of the evil in our town.</i>

108
00:05:16,024 --> 00:05:18,234
-What did you find?
-This.

109
00:05:27,368 --> 00:05:30,455
So the Ardientes promised
to give the land to the farmers.

110
00:05:30,997 --> 00:05:33,499
But they weren't able to transfer it

111
00:05:33,583 --> 00:05:34,959
under the farmers' name.

112
00:05:35,043 --> 00:05:36,085
The farmers never thought the Ardientes

113
00:05:36,169 --> 00:05:38,212
would take it back, but they did.

114
00:05:39,047 --> 00:05:40,506
Listen to me, Ivy.

115
00:05:40,590 --> 00:05:42,467
You don't have to do anything.

116
00:05:42,550 --> 00:05:45,094
I can gather evidence by myself.

117
00:05:45,178 --> 00:05:46,471
Just leave everything to me.

118
00:05:47,055 --> 00:05:48,431
I don't want you
putting yourself in danger.

119
00:05:48,514 --> 00:05:51,184
-I can take care of myself.
-I know that. I do.

120
00:05:51,267 --> 00:05:52,727
But don't you see how evil Emilia is?

121
00:05:52,810 --> 00:05:54,312
You saw the news.

122
00:05:54,812 --> 00:05:56,230
She had that man killed.

123
00:05:56,898 --> 00:06:00,026
They're willing to take anyone
down just to clear their name.

124
00:06:00,109 --> 00:06:02,236
So don't mingle with those devils.

125
00:06:02,320 --> 00:06:04,489
How will I get justice for my family…

126
00:06:05,656 --> 00:06:07,658
if I act like a coward?

127
00:06:25,593 --> 00:06:28,429
[tense music playing]

128
00:06:39,357 --> 00:06:42,068
Madrigal, are you done with
the errands I told you to run?

129
00:06:42,151 --> 00:06:43,152
Yes, Mayor.

130
00:06:53,371 --> 00:06:54,372
[Arnaldo] Ms. Aguas.

131
00:06:55,164 --> 00:06:57,208
-Mr. Mayor.
-Congratulations.

132
00:06:57,291 --> 00:06:59,168
The Governor's launching the project.

133
00:06:59,252 --> 00:07:01,587
Well, thanks to you.

134
00:07:01,671 --> 00:07:04,173
You're the one who convinced me to invest,

135
00:07:04,257 --> 00:07:06,801
and stay here in Ardiente.

136
00:07:07,844 --> 00:07:09,178
-Cheers.
-Cheers.

137
00:07:13,516 --> 00:07:17,895
-Babe! I missed you.
-Hey.

138
00:07:22,024 --> 00:07:23,359
Oh. [chuckles]

139
00:07:23,860 --> 00:07:24,861
Miss Aguas.

140
00:07:26,237 --> 00:07:27,238
Hello.

141
00:07:29,323 --> 00:07:30,324
How are you?

142
00:07:31,075 --> 00:07:32,535
Enjoying the view.

143
00:07:32,618 --> 00:07:35,788
And of course, enjoying
my new partnership with Arnaldo.

144
00:07:36,330 --> 00:07:38,458
[Natalie laughs]

145
00:07:38,541 --> 00:07:41,461
You know, Arnaldo really knows

146
00:07:41,544 --> 00:07:46,090
how to use opportunities to his advantage.

147
00:07:46,174 --> 00:07:49,469
Like that barren land.

148
00:07:49,552 --> 00:07:53,431
Those farmers there are like leeches

149
00:07:53,514 --> 00:07:57,393
sucking the nutrients from
a land that isn't even theirs.

150
00:07:59,061 --> 00:08:03,566
And like your coming here.

151
00:08:04,108 --> 00:08:06,402
There's this new girl in town,

152
00:08:06,486 --> 00:08:09,780
and suddenly, there's a partnership!

153
00:08:09,989 --> 00:08:12,074
[Natalie laughs]

154
00:08:12,158 --> 00:08:16,370
Arnaldo, this means
that Natalie is really happy

155
00:08:16,454 --> 00:08:19,207
that I invested here in Ardiente.

156
00:08:19,457 --> 00:08:20,791
[laughs]

157
00:08:20,875 --> 00:08:24,295
Ivy, don't get ahead of yourself.

158
00:08:24,378 --> 00:08:26,339
I'm just saying that I'm happy.

159
00:08:26,422 --> 00:08:30,384
And I'll stay happy if you stay here

160
00:08:30,468 --> 00:08:33,221
strictly because of business.

161
00:08:35,973 --> 00:08:37,600
And what if I don't?

162
00:08:43,105 --> 00:08:44,565
No worries, Natalie.

163
00:08:45,566 --> 00:08:49,445
I never mix business with pleasure.

164
00:08:50,029 --> 00:08:50,988
Do you understand?

165
00:08:52,156 --> 00:08:53,449
[laughs]

166
00:08:53,533 --> 00:08:54,909
Oh, you're so cute.

167
00:08:55,451 --> 00:08:56,744
I'm thirsty.

168
00:08:57,036 --> 00:08:58,579
Can you get me a glass of wine?

169
00:08:58,955 --> 00:09:00,164
Yeah. Sure.

170
00:09:00,748 --> 00:09:03,668
Or better yet, I'll go with you. Let's go.

171
00:09:04,460 --> 00:09:05,461
Okay.

172
00:09:05,836 --> 00:09:06,837
[Natalie giggles]

173
00:09:08,339 --> 00:09:09,382
[Natalie] Smile, baby.

174
00:09:23,646 --> 00:09:24,397
Hey.

175
00:09:24,480 --> 00:09:26,941
I didn't know all of Mom's
supporters would be here.

176
00:09:27,483 --> 00:09:28,776
Even that Ivy Aguas.

177
00:09:30,444 --> 00:09:31,946
Dad, I'll be off now.

178
00:09:32,029 --> 00:09:34,073
Hold on. Where are you going?
We still have to--

179
00:09:34,156 --> 00:09:36,784
I don't want to hear anything
about the EPZ.

180
00:09:38,244 --> 00:09:39,161
Listen, Diego.

181
00:09:39,245 --> 00:09:41,038
You're an Ardiente,
that's why you're here.

182
00:09:41,455 --> 00:09:44,250
Sometimes, you have to do
things you don't want to.

183
00:09:44,750 --> 00:09:48,045
That's one of the consequences
of being part of this family.

184
00:09:49,589 --> 00:09:50,590
Sorry, Dad.

185
00:10:00,349 --> 00:10:01,809
What took you so long?

186
00:10:02,602 --> 00:10:05,438
The reception was terrible
at the place I was.

187
00:10:05,646 --> 00:10:07,565
And where was that? Timbuktu?

188
00:10:08,649 --> 00:10:10,484
Let's go.

189
00:10:10,568 --> 00:10:14,488
-[Emilia] Hi, friends!
-[applause]

190
00:10:14,572 --> 00:10:18,993
-[Emilia] Hello! Ivy. Hi!
-[applause]

191
00:10:19,076 --> 00:10:23,581
<i>You're so happy right now,</i>
<i>Emilia. Enjoy it while it lasts.</i>

192
00:10:24,248 --> 00:10:26,250
[Filipino folk music playing]

193
00:11:13,839 --> 00:11:15,800
[applause]

194
00:11:23,599 --> 00:11:26,769
Thank you very much,
Folklorico Dance Company.

195
00:11:27,937 --> 00:11:32,733
Let's not beat around the bush.
Here is our beloved governor,

196
00:11:32,817 --> 00:11:36,487
Governor Emilia Ardiente-Torillo.

197
00:11:36,570 --> 00:11:38,572
[applause]

198
00:11:44,286 --> 00:11:46,497
A pleasant evening to everyone!

199
00:11:46,580 --> 00:11:48,290
My friends!

200
00:11:55,464 --> 00:11:58,342
I don't know where to start.

201
00:11:59,176 --> 00:12:01,971
I'm sure everyone here knows about

202
00:12:02,054 --> 00:12:06,851
our dear Congressman Julio
Ardiente's condition.

203
00:12:08,352 --> 00:12:09,228
[Emilia sobs]

204
00:12:14,567 --> 00:12:15,776
It's okay. It's okay.

205
00:12:15,985 --> 00:12:18,070
[applause]

206
00:12:30,958 --> 00:12:35,337
I'm very thankful for
my husband, Mr. Raul Torillo.

207
00:12:39,175 --> 00:12:43,262
My father is currently in the U.S.

208
00:12:43,345 --> 00:12:47,558
to recover and is accompanied
by his trusted aide.

209
00:12:47,850 --> 00:12:52,730
But this is the proper moment
for all of us to unite

210
00:12:52,813 --> 00:12:56,609
for Poblacion Ardiente
and for Señor Julio Ardiente!

211
00:12:56,692 --> 00:12:59,153
[applause]

212
00:12:59,236 --> 00:13:00,488
[Emilia] You know what they say.

213
00:13:00,571 --> 00:13:04,158
While there's life,
there's hope and happiness.

214
00:13:04,825 --> 00:13:06,660
Because I am still here

215
00:13:06,744 --> 00:13:10,581
as your mother and governor of this town.

216
00:13:11,248 --> 00:13:14,543
And I want you to call me Mommy Emilia…

217
00:13:15,753 --> 00:13:17,630
the mother of this town!

218
00:13:17,713 --> 00:13:18,756
[applause]

219
00:13:18,839 --> 00:13:25,012
And for my first ever project
as mother of this town,

220
00:13:25,095 --> 00:13:30,434
let me introduce to you
a good friend of mine.

221
00:13:30,518 --> 00:13:34,772
I took her on as a consultant
for my EPZ project.

222
00:13:35,773 --> 00:13:40,486
I wish to introduce to you,
Miss Ivy Aguas!

223
00:13:40,569 --> 00:13:42,571
[applause]

224
00:13:45,241 --> 00:13:47,952
Ivy, come join me.

225
00:14:07,972 --> 00:14:08,973
Thank you.

226
00:14:10,015 --> 00:14:11,100
Ivy.

227
00:14:12,351 --> 00:14:13,686
[both chuckle]

228
00:14:14,311 --> 00:14:16,021
Governor Emilia.

229
00:14:17,815 --> 00:14:21,151
You know, our governor
here loves surprises.

230
00:14:22,820 --> 00:14:25,322
Don't we all love surprises, Ivy?

231
00:14:25,406 --> 00:14:29,201
It's better than being surprised.

232
00:14:29,285 --> 00:14:31,579
I might have a heart attack like Papa.

233
00:14:31,662 --> 00:14:34,540
[laughs]

234
00:14:34,623 --> 00:14:38,377
You know, at least now,
your plans will push through.

235
00:14:38,794 --> 00:14:39,879
Our plans.

236
00:14:42,172 --> 00:14:45,092
You're not alone, Governor. You're right.

237
00:14:45,175 --> 00:14:47,428
I should let go of my cheap sentiments,

238
00:14:47,511 --> 00:14:49,972
so I can get what I want.

239
00:14:50,973 --> 00:14:53,183
So, is it a yes?

240
00:14:54,018 --> 00:14:55,019
Yes.

241
00:14:56,103 --> 00:15:01,358
Great! Great!
Two women uniting for a cause.

242
00:15:01,442 --> 00:15:04,862
Ivy, for… for Señor Julio!

243
00:15:05,571 --> 00:15:07,197
For Poblacion Ardiente.

244
00:15:07,281 --> 00:15:09,283
[applause]

245
00:15:19,543 --> 00:15:20,544
Senator.

246
00:15:21,378 --> 00:15:23,631
-Hi. Excuse me.
-Sure.

247
00:15:23,839 --> 00:15:24,840
Emilia.

248
00:15:27,092 --> 00:15:29,011
Fancy seeing you here, Senator.

249
00:15:29,094 --> 00:15:31,513
Congratulations, Emilia.

250
00:15:31,597 --> 00:15:36,727
I'm hoping for the success
of your leadership of this town

251
00:15:36,810 --> 00:15:39,229
while Julio is recovering.

252
00:15:39,939 --> 00:15:42,608
Thank you, Senator.
I hope you really mean that.

253
00:15:42,816 --> 00:15:44,276
'Cause it would mean so much to me.

254
00:15:44,902 --> 00:15:46,737
Of course, Emilia.

255
00:15:46,820 --> 00:15:48,781
What's the purpose
of the long-standing friendship

256
00:15:48,864 --> 00:15:52,326
between our families if not for that?

257
00:15:53,035 --> 00:15:53,994
I know.

258
00:15:54,078 --> 00:15:56,580
Our families have been friends
for the longest time.

259
00:15:57,373 --> 00:15:59,875
And I do believe

260
00:15:59,959 --> 00:16:04,421
that you find your true friends
in times of crisis, Senator.

261
00:16:04,964 --> 00:16:06,548
I couldn't agree more.

262
00:16:08,968 --> 00:16:09,969
Thank you.

263
00:16:15,933 --> 00:16:19,061
-Senator Pablo.
-Miss Aguas.

264
00:16:19,770 --> 00:16:21,814
Senator, I'll leave you with Miss Aguas.

265
00:16:21,897 --> 00:16:23,482
-Excuse me.
-Thank you, Emilia.

266
00:16:24,066 --> 00:16:25,275
-Madam, the press is waiting.
-Okay.

267
00:16:25,359 --> 00:16:26,944
[Ivy] Senator.

268
00:16:27,027 --> 00:16:28,737
Good evening. Good evening.

269
00:16:28,821 --> 00:16:30,823
Is it true that you'll be
running for senator

270
00:16:30,906 --> 00:16:32,449
in your father's place?

271
00:16:32,533 --> 00:16:33,993
I'm just proving that

272
00:16:34,076 --> 00:16:37,287
the people of Poblacion Ardiente
have nothing to fear

273
00:16:37,371 --> 00:16:39,873
in my father's temporary absence,

274
00:16:39,957 --> 00:16:42,501
because I am capable of taking over.

275
00:16:42,835 --> 00:16:44,753
I am the mother of this town,

276
00:16:44,837 --> 00:16:47,589
so I will make sure our town is safe.

277
00:16:47,673 --> 00:16:49,675
-[applause]
-Thank you.

278
00:16:54,263 --> 00:16:58,142
I see that you're still siding
with the Ardientes, Senator.

279
00:16:59,852 --> 00:17:01,854
What was that you said at the party?

280
00:17:02,354 --> 00:17:07,067
Politics is about making
friends, finding your allies,

281
00:17:07,151 --> 00:17:10,112
and destroying your enemies.

282
00:17:12,072 --> 00:17:15,576
Well, look at you,
you're Emilia's consultant now.

283
00:17:18,579 --> 00:17:21,874
We politicians know that game well.

284
00:17:22,750 --> 00:17:28,172
I am still Emilia's ally,
and we will clean up this mess.

285
00:17:29,173 --> 00:17:33,594
But you, I wonder.
What's your game, Miss Aguas?

286
00:17:39,516 --> 00:17:45,230
If I tell you, you might not
want to play anymore, Senator.

287
00:17:45,314 --> 00:17:48,567
[tense music playing]

288
00:18:06,168 --> 00:18:07,377
-[Loring] There.
-Miss Loring.

289
00:18:07,461 --> 00:18:09,046
[Loring] Oh, thank you.

290
00:18:09,129 --> 00:18:10,089
Miss Loring.

291
00:18:10,172 --> 00:18:13,675
Oh, Miss Ivy, it's you!

292
00:18:13,759 --> 00:18:14,802
Do you still have banana fritters?

293
00:18:14,885 --> 00:18:16,011
Can I buy some?

294
00:18:16,095 --> 00:18:18,680
Yes, ma'am.
Do you really want to buy them?

295
00:18:18,764 --> 00:18:21,100
Yes. I'll buy all of them.

296
00:18:21,183 --> 00:18:25,854
That's a lot. Aren't you on a diet?

297
00:18:25,938 --> 00:18:27,606
-Not anymore.
-[Diego] Nanny, let's go.

298
00:18:27,689 --> 00:18:29,358
I'll drive you to town.

299
00:18:29,900 --> 00:18:30,901
[Loring] Ah…

300
00:18:31,276 --> 00:18:34,780
Don't worry about the change.
It's an advance for next time.

301
00:18:34,863 --> 00:18:36,198
-But…
-Just keep it for now.

302
00:18:36,281 --> 00:18:37,783
-But…
-Miss Aguas.

303
00:18:38,784 --> 00:18:39,618
Mr. Torillo.

304
00:18:39,701 --> 00:18:42,704
Let me just get a bag for this.
I'll be quick.

305
00:18:42,788 --> 00:18:44,373
-Thank you.
-Thank you, too.

306
00:18:47,459 --> 00:18:49,044
Congratulations, by the way.

307
00:18:49,962 --> 00:18:52,381
You were chosen as one
of Mama's consultants,

308
00:18:52,464 --> 00:18:53,799
and your project is pushing through.

309
00:18:54,800 --> 00:18:58,387
The last time we spoke,
didn't you tell me you'd stop?

310
00:18:58,470 --> 00:19:01,682
Well, Mr. Torillo, as a businesswoman…

311
00:19:02,432 --> 00:19:03,725
I studied the proposal carefully.

312
00:19:03,809 --> 00:19:09,606
And I realized that the EPZ will
greatly benefit the farmers,

313
00:19:10,023 --> 00:19:12,067
and all of Poblacion Ardiente.

314
00:19:12,151 --> 00:19:13,944
You're oblivious, Miss Aguas.

315
00:19:14,611 --> 00:19:16,196
That's the problem with people like you.

316
00:19:16,488 --> 00:19:18,657
You see the poor as ants.

317
00:19:19,283 --> 00:19:21,368
You think that their lives
will instantly change,

318
00:19:21,451 --> 00:19:23,245
at the snap of your fingers.

319
00:19:23,745 --> 00:19:26,582
Mr. Torillo, you're oblivious, too.

320
00:19:35,465 --> 00:19:38,760
Miss Ivy, here are your fritters.

321
00:19:38,844 --> 00:19:40,679
-Thank you, Miss Loring.
-For the rest of them--

322
00:19:40,762 --> 00:19:44,349
-I'll get them next time.
-Okay. Thank you!

323
00:19:52,941 --> 00:19:57,237
Senator, thank you for
helping us clear our name.

324
00:19:58,155 --> 00:20:01,575
I'm just giving back the favor.
Thank you for the trust, Emilia.

325
00:20:04,494 --> 00:20:09,291
Um, Senator, since our name
has been cleared of all issues,

326
00:20:09,374 --> 00:20:11,793
maybe you can promote me in our party

327
00:20:11,877 --> 00:20:15,088
as a replacement candidate
for Papa's senatorial bid.

328
00:20:15,547 --> 00:20:16,548
[scoffs]

329
00:20:16,965 --> 00:20:21,553
I knew it. Your friendship
comes with a price.

330
00:20:23,263 --> 00:20:27,142
Seriously? You want to run for the Senate?

331
00:20:28,393 --> 00:20:32,356
Senator, you're one of the most
influential people in the party.

332
00:20:32,773 --> 00:20:34,441
Maybe you can vouch for me?

333
00:20:34,524 --> 00:20:36,318
It's too early to tell.

334
00:20:36,902 --> 00:20:38,695
Besides, the party
highly respects the opinions

335
00:20:38,779 --> 00:20:40,948
of Senator Magno and Senator Jose.

336
00:20:41,031 --> 00:20:44,201
They're the ones with the final say.

337
00:20:46,453 --> 00:20:49,456
I see. Natalie, you should eat.

338
00:20:49,539 --> 00:20:50,457
Yeah.

339
00:20:58,465 --> 00:21:01,051
[grunting]

340
00:21:05,055 --> 00:21:06,974
[Diego] <i>You're oblivious, Ms. Aguas.</i>

341
00:21:07,557 --> 00:21:09,017
<i>That's the problem with people like you.</i>

342
00:21:09,434 --> 00:21:11,645
<i>You see the poor as ants.</i>

343
00:21:12,145 --> 00:21:14,273
<i>You think that their lives will change</i>

344
00:21:14,356 --> 00:21:16,149
<i>at the snap of your fingers.</i>

345
00:21:16,650 --> 00:21:19,194
[Ivy] <i>Mr. Torillo, you're oblivious, too.</i>

346
00:21:19,278 --> 00:21:20,779
[grunting]

347
00:21:27,786 --> 00:21:28,704
[grunts]

348
00:21:28,787 --> 00:21:29,788
[shouts]

349
00:21:34,209 --> 00:21:36,586
That woman just won't give in.

350
00:21:36,920 --> 00:21:39,381
She's the reason
you're going to lose your land.

351
00:21:39,506 --> 00:21:41,258
What should we do now?

352
00:21:41,967 --> 00:21:43,260
Are we just going to sit here

353
00:21:43,343 --> 00:21:44,886
while they take our land from us?

354
00:21:46,847 --> 00:21:47,806
[shouts]

355
00:21:49,057 --> 00:21:52,102
If I could just tell them
what I'm going through.

356
00:21:54,479 --> 00:21:57,566
If only I could tell them
how evil the Ardientes are…

357
00:21:58,900 --> 00:22:03,864
and about everything
they did to me and my family.

358
00:22:03,947 --> 00:22:05,449
I'd shout it out!

359
00:22:06,158 --> 00:22:08,285
I want everyone to know, especially Diego,

360
00:22:08,368 --> 00:22:10,787
that I'm not just a rich businesswoman!

361
00:22:11,580 --> 00:22:13,623
I'm a victim of his family, too.

362
00:22:13,915 --> 00:22:18,670
[Ramon] Why are you always
blaming the Ardientes?

363
00:22:18,754 --> 00:22:19,838
And you, Diego,

364
00:22:19,921 --> 00:22:22,382
why are you always
going against your family?

365
00:22:22,466 --> 00:22:23,842
Aren't you an Ardiente, too?

366
00:22:23,967 --> 00:22:26,636
Mister Ramon, I don't want
to go against them.

367
00:22:26,720 --> 00:22:29,097
I just can't accept
that my family pushed through

368
00:22:29,181 --> 00:22:31,433
with the EPZ
all because of that Ivy Aguas!

369
00:22:31,516 --> 00:22:34,644
I want to tell Diego
the truth that it's me.

370
00:22:34,728 --> 00:22:37,814
I'm Lily, I'm your friend.

371
00:22:39,775 --> 00:22:42,069
But of course, I can't do that.

372
00:22:42,778 --> 00:22:45,781
This is her fault. And now what?

373
00:22:46,239 --> 00:22:49,034
She tricked us all by giving
the go signal for the project.

374
00:22:49,117 --> 00:22:50,577
We have to fight back.

375
00:22:54,164 --> 00:22:56,750
[Carlotta] If this is weighing
you down, just remember

376
00:22:56,833 --> 00:22:59,836
whom you're doing this for.

377
00:23:01,546 --> 00:23:03,340
Nanny, I know that.

378
00:23:06,468 --> 00:23:07,969
And I'll never forget that.

379
00:23:09,679 --> 00:23:12,140
Tomorrow, I'll go to Emilia.

380
00:23:13,683 --> 00:23:15,477
And I will make her feel

381
00:23:15,560 --> 00:23:20,148
that Ivy Aguas is still her trusted ally.

382
00:23:26,738 --> 00:23:30,283
[ominous music playing]

383
00:23:40,043 --> 00:23:43,088
-[birds chirping]
-[suspenseful music playing]

384
00:24:32,053 --> 00:24:33,513
[man] Turn left, go straight ahead,

385
00:24:33,597 --> 00:24:34,598
and you'll see the governor's office.

386
00:24:34,681 --> 00:24:35,682
[Ivy] Thank you.

387
00:24:55,160 --> 00:24:58,955
Jasmin, I'll be going
to the market real quick.

388
00:24:59,039 --> 00:25:00,040
Stay here--

389
00:25:01,041 --> 00:25:02,042
Jasmin?

390
00:25:05,170 --> 00:25:06,171
Jasmin?

391
00:25:08,048 --> 00:25:09,049
Jasmin?

392
00:25:14,471 --> 00:25:15,472
Jasmin!

393
00:25:16,556 --> 00:25:20,435
Where'd she go? Jasmin?! Jasmin?!

394
00:25:21,436 --> 00:25:23,730
My goodness. Where'd she go?

395
00:25:23,813 --> 00:25:24,814
Jasmin?!

396
00:25:26,691 --> 00:25:27,692
Jasmin?!

397
00:25:38,954 --> 00:25:40,580
It's a good thing you were able

398
00:25:40,664 --> 00:25:42,749
to clear my name from that scandal.

399
00:25:43,375 --> 00:25:45,210
Don't flatter yourself, Raul.

400
00:25:45,669 --> 00:25:48,797
You're part of this family,
so I was obligated to help you.

401
00:25:50,840 --> 00:25:52,968
And always remember

402
00:25:53,051 --> 00:25:55,804
that I'm the reason
you aren't rotting in jail.

403
00:25:56,554 --> 00:25:58,181
I have you on a tight leash.

404
00:26:01,518 --> 00:26:02,811
Jasmin?!

405
00:26:03,937 --> 00:26:06,231
Where are you, Jasmin?!

406
00:26:11,820 --> 00:26:13,822
[bleak instrumental playing]

407
00:26:19,828 --> 00:26:20,870
[Belen sighs]

408
00:26:23,248 --> 00:26:26,251
[phone ringing]

409
00:26:34,259 --> 00:26:35,969
I need to take this call.

410
00:26:42,851 --> 00:26:45,270
Hello, Auntie? Why did you call?

411
00:26:45,353 --> 00:26:47,480
Raul, it's Jasmin…

412
00:26:47,939 --> 00:26:49,566
Why? What happened to Jasmin?

413
00:26:51,359 --> 00:26:54,321
She's gone. I've searched
the whole house for her.

414
00:26:54,404 --> 00:26:57,073
Auntie, didn't I say to keep
an eye on her at all times?

415
00:26:57,157 --> 00:26:58,783
You can't leave her by herself.

416
00:27:00,118 --> 00:27:03,038
Auntie? Hello? Hello?

417
00:27:03,121 --> 00:27:06,624
[tense music playing]

418
00:27:19,763 --> 00:27:22,223
Where could she be? Jasmin!

419
00:27:27,020 --> 00:27:28,229
Jasmin!

420
00:27:31,566 --> 00:27:32,650
Jasmin!

421
00:27:33,818 --> 00:27:37,572
Oh, no! Oh, my! Look at you!

422
00:27:37,655 --> 00:27:38,823
What are you doing?

423
00:27:38,907 --> 00:27:42,077
I almost had a heart attack!

424
00:27:42,952 --> 00:27:46,206
Let me see! Oh, my goodness!

425
00:27:46,498 --> 00:27:48,500
Come, let's go home!

426
00:27:51,252 --> 00:27:52,295
Be careful!

427
00:27:52,379 --> 00:27:54,672
Let's go! Goodness.

428
00:27:55,465 --> 00:27:57,258
-[phone ringing]
-Wait a second.

429
00:27:59,344 --> 00:28:00,678
Hello. Raul.

430
00:28:00,762 --> 00:28:04,265
Hello, Auntie? What happened?
Have you found her?

431
00:28:04,349 --> 00:28:07,435
Yes, she's with me.
She almost fell off a cliff.

432
00:28:07,811 --> 00:28:09,687
<i>But don't worry, she's safe now.</i>

433
00:28:09,771 --> 00:28:12,357
How did she end up near a cliff?

434
00:28:12,649 --> 00:28:16,486
Auntie, I entrusted her to you.

435
00:28:16,569 --> 00:28:18,321
Please be more careful next time.

436
00:28:19,781 --> 00:28:20,865
Okay, okay. Never mind.

437
00:28:20,949 --> 00:28:23,868
I'll find a way to head
back there as soon as possible.

438
00:28:28,206 --> 00:28:29,791
[Belen] <i>All right. We'll wait for you.</i>

439
00:28:34,671 --> 00:28:36,131
Hi, Mr. Torillo.

440
00:28:36,548 --> 00:28:38,925
You look… tense.

441
00:28:40,051 --> 00:28:42,637
Miss Aguas. Have you been there long?

442
00:28:43,847 --> 00:28:46,933
Yes. What about you?

443
00:28:47,392 --> 00:28:50,270
Do you have an appointment somewhere?

444
00:28:50,770 --> 00:28:54,858
From the tone of your voice,
it sounds like an emergency.

445
00:29:07,078 --> 00:29:09,539
It's nothing. It's just…

446
00:29:10,749 --> 00:29:14,711
it's just that some of my men
are stealing from me.

447
00:29:15,170 --> 00:29:17,964
I asked my aunt to watch over them.

448
00:29:18,590 --> 00:29:24,179
They're being such a nuisance.
It's difficult to trust them.

449
00:29:27,348 --> 00:29:28,725
So you better be careful.

450
00:29:37,233 --> 00:29:39,569
Ivy? Oh, Raul.

451
00:29:39,652 --> 00:29:40,653
Emilia.

452
00:29:41,446 --> 00:29:42,655
What are you doing here?

453
00:29:43,573 --> 00:29:46,284
Um. I was just asking Mr. Torillo

454
00:29:46,367 --> 00:29:49,078
where your office was, but here it is.

455
00:29:50,079 --> 00:29:51,498
So, let's go?

456
00:29:52,749 --> 00:29:56,044
Okay. Raul, let's go.

457
00:30:07,806 --> 00:30:10,225
I just want to be certain

458
00:30:10,308 --> 00:30:13,561
the land will be strategic
for our purposes.

459
00:30:13,645 --> 00:30:17,148
Maybe I should visit the site.

460
00:30:22,987 --> 00:30:23,988
Emilia?

461
00:30:25,281 --> 00:30:27,075
Emilia, did you hear what I just said?

462
00:30:27,992 --> 00:30:31,788
Oh. Yes. Do what you think is right.

463
00:30:31,871 --> 00:30:35,792
I trust your judgment.
But please do it ASAP, okay?

464
00:30:41,130 --> 00:30:42,632
Don't worry, Emilia.

465
00:30:43,132 --> 00:30:47,470
I always make sure that
I finish everything I start.

466
00:30:47,971 --> 00:30:48,972
Good.

467
00:30:51,516 --> 00:30:53,518
-I have to go.
-Okay.

468
00:30:54,894 --> 00:30:56,271
-Bye, Ivy.
-Bye.

469
00:30:56,354 --> 00:30:57,397
I'll take you there.

470
00:30:59,107 --> 00:31:00,817
-Mr. Torillo.
-Yeah.

471
00:31:01,818 --> 00:31:02,819
Bye.

472
00:31:06,656 --> 00:31:07,657
Bye.

473
00:31:12,537 --> 00:31:13,872
Where are you going?

474
00:31:13,955 --> 00:31:14,998
I'm going out. I have errands--

475
00:31:15,081 --> 00:31:17,542
Whoever you were talking to can wait. Sit.

476
00:31:19,168 --> 00:31:20,169
I'm leaving.

477
00:31:20,712 --> 00:31:23,882
[tense music playing]

478
00:32:18,686 --> 00:32:21,272
<i>Let's see if you can</i>
<i>still hide from me, Raul.</i>

479
00:32:24,359 --> 00:32:27,987
<i>If you think you can fool me</i>
<i>again, then you're mistaken.</i>

480
00:32:28,529 --> 00:32:29,739
<i>Not this time.</i>

481
00:33:01,145 --> 00:33:02,188
Miss Aguas.

482
00:33:03,481 --> 00:33:06,109
Mr. Mayor, what are you doing here?

483
00:33:07,193 --> 00:33:10,780
Well, I heard you were coming
here, so I decided to drop by.

484
00:33:11,781 --> 00:33:14,701
Aside from the fact
that I always want to see you,

485
00:33:14,784 --> 00:33:15,952
I brought something with me.

486
00:33:18,663 --> 00:33:21,249
In less than a month, we can get
these farmers out of here.

487
00:33:23,543 --> 00:33:26,045
Isn't that great news? Let's go.

488
00:33:50,570 --> 00:33:53,573
Hey, man. Just one rooster today?

489
00:33:53,656 --> 00:33:55,742
Yes, sir. It's the best cock
we have here, sir.

490
00:33:55,825 --> 00:33:57,076
-All right.
-That's a sure winner, sir.

491
00:33:57,160 --> 00:33:59,579
I'll just come back for it
next time, all right?

492
00:33:59,662 --> 00:34:02,081
I came by unannounced, so…

493
00:34:02,165 --> 00:34:03,458
Good morning, Governor.

494
00:34:05,168 --> 00:34:06,210
Good morning.

495
00:34:06,878 --> 00:34:10,173
All right, man. I'll call you again.

496
00:34:15,470 --> 00:34:16,637
What are you doing here?

497
00:34:17,513 --> 00:34:21,809
Raul, who's the woman
you've been coming here for?

498
00:34:21,893 --> 00:34:24,520
Where is she? Bring her out.

499
00:34:25,772 --> 00:34:27,231
What are you talking about, Emilia?

500
00:34:28,649 --> 00:34:30,151
Raul, don't try to deny it.

501
00:34:30,818 --> 00:34:32,278
Where is your other woman?

502
00:34:32,487 --> 00:34:34,697
Where is she? Where is Ivy?

503
00:34:35,823 --> 00:34:38,367
What the-- What woman
are you talking about?

504
00:34:38,451 --> 00:34:41,079
Emilia, why don't you go see a doctor?

505
00:34:41,162 --> 00:34:43,414
Because it sounds like you've gone nuts.

506
00:34:43,581 --> 00:34:45,750
I'm here for the roosters
I was telling you about

507
00:34:45,833 --> 00:34:48,086
for my cockfighting business.

508
00:34:48,169 --> 00:34:49,003
That's why I'm here.

509
00:34:49,087 --> 00:34:50,588
Didn't you see I was talking to a man?

510
00:34:50,671 --> 00:34:53,132
Raul, don't try to act dumb.

511
00:34:53,508 --> 00:34:56,344
Did you think I wouldn't notice
how you and Ivy were talking?

512
00:34:56,427 --> 00:34:58,137
Your son likes her.

513
00:34:58,221 --> 00:35:00,807
I'm not interested in that woman.

514
00:35:01,265 --> 00:35:03,476
What if he didn't? You'd make a move then?

515
00:35:03,726 --> 00:35:04,685
[scoffs]

516
00:35:05,353 --> 00:35:07,105
Whatever, you're impossible.

517
00:35:08,439 --> 00:35:09,565
Raul.

518
00:35:09,649 --> 00:35:12,026
Just bring out your other woman.
I know she exists.

519
00:35:12,110 --> 00:35:15,196
Where did you go when I kicked you out?

520
00:35:15,279 --> 00:35:17,156
And who were you talking to on the phone?

521
00:35:18,407 --> 00:35:19,408
No one.

522
00:35:20,576 --> 00:35:23,663
So, you still don't know
what I'm capable of.

523
00:35:24,747 --> 00:35:26,749
Do you know that I can finish you off

524
00:35:26,833 --> 00:35:29,669
and have your woman
buried six feet under with you?

525
00:35:30,461 --> 00:35:34,465
Try to leave.
You'll see what I can really do.

526
00:35:39,470 --> 00:35:41,180
-[man] Hi, Mayor.
-[woman] Good morning.

527
00:35:41,264 --> 00:35:42,890
[Arnaldo] Good morning.

528
00:35:42,974 --> 00:35:44,642
[man 2] You're early today, Mayor.

529
00:35:44,725 --> 00:35:46,477
I know. I just wanted to drop by.

530
00:35:46,561 --> 00:35:48,146
These vegetables look delicious.

531
00:35:48,229 --> 00:35:50,481
[woman] Yes. Our crops are always fresh.

532
00:35:50,565 --> 00:35:52,441
I'm glad you had time for this.

533
00:35:53,109 --> 00:35:55,361
I thought you had a lot of engagements.

534
00:35:55,444 --> 00:35:58,197
I blocked them all off to be with you.

535
00:36:00,158 --> 00:36:03,202
Mr. Mayor, about the eviction notice…

536
00:36:03,953 --> 00:36:07,165
Isn't the time frame
you gave them too short?

537
00:36:07,248 --> 00:36:09,584
Where do you plan
to relocate these people?

538
00:36:09,667 --> 00:36:11,127
What about their livelihoods?

539
00:36:12,461 --> 00:36:14,672
Ms. Aguas, everything's been planned out.

540
00:36:15,798 --> 00:36:16,757
Don't worry.

541
00:36:18,551 --> 00:36:19,552
Let's go?

542
00:36:26,475 --> 00:36:28,311
How is the Congressman's health?

543
00:36:28,895 --> 00:36:31,189
I just spoke to Papa's doctor, Senator.

544
00:36:32,106 --> 00:36:33,441
He still needs to recover.

545
00:36:33,524 --> 00:36:36,068
And I don't think he can handle
the stress of the campaign.

546
00:36:36,152 --> 00:36:39,030
So, goodbye Julio for senator.
That's too bad.

547
00:36:39,113 --> 00:36:40,781
Arnaldo has the leadership capability

548
00:36:40,865 --> 00:36:45,161
and the whole package,
but he still has a lot to learn.

549
00:36:45,536 --> 00:36:48,247
We need someone more
experienced to run for senator.

550
00:36:48,331 --> 00:36:49,373
[clears throat]

551
00:36:49,457 --> 00:36:51,167
One who knows the game well,

552
00:36:51,250 --> 00:36:54,337
has the authority, has a good image,

553
00:36:54,420 --> 00:36:55,588
and most importantly,

554
00:36:55,671 --> 00:36:58,007
one who can definitely get people's votes.

555
00:36:58,382 --> 00:37:01,177
Why not Emilia?

556
00:37:05,806 --> 00:37:08,601
Well, senators, I've been
serving my constituents

557
00:37:08,684 --> 00:37:09,977
for the past 10 years.

558
00:37:10,394 --> 00:37:14,065
And in the game of politics, I always win.

559
00:37:14,815 --> 00:37:15,942
[Magno] Yes, that's true.

560
00:37:16,317 --> 00:37:18,069
But, no offense Emilia…

561
00:37:18,903 --> 00:37:21,155
there are things about your credentials,

562
00:37:21,239 --> 00:37:22,949
which we find lacking.

563
00:37:23,866 --> 00:37:26,827
Your father is a known
politician on a national scale.

564
00:37:26,911 --> 00:37:29,914
If you can't reach
Julio's level of influence,

565
00:37:29,997 --> 00:37:32,208
by the time the campaign period starts,

566
00:37:32,291 --> 00:37:34,168
you'll only be wasting time and money.

567
00:37:34,252 --> 00:37:35,753
Because you'll surely lose.

568
00:37:35,836 --> 00:37:37,880
[tense music playing]

569
00:37:49,058 --> 00:37:51,060
-[woman] There you go.
-[man] The mayor's here!

570
00:37:51,143 --> 00:37:52,353
[man 2] Oh. It's the mayor. The mayor.

571
00:37:52,436 --> 00:37:53,271
[woman 2] The mayor.

572
00:37:53,354 --> 00:37:55,398
[Loring] Oh. Wait, wait. Careful.

573
00:37:55,481 --> 00:37:57,149
[woman] You dropped the eggplants.

574
00:37:57,233 --> 00:37:58,567
[Fernan] Mayor, Miss Ivy…

575
00:37:58,651 --> 00:38:00,695
-[man 3] Good afternoon.
-What brings you…

576
00:38:00,778 --> 00:38:02,363
-to our place?
-[man 4] Good afternoon.

577
00:38:03,155 --> 00:38:04,824
[Nimfa] Hi, Mayor Arnaldo!

578
00:38:04,907 --> 00:38:08,744
You're so handsome, just like Diego.

579
00:38:08,828 --> 00:38:12,498
Ah… I guess it runs in the family.

580
00:38:13,791 --> 00:38:17,795
Hey, your father
is handsome, too! See that?

581
00:38:17,878 --> 00:38:19,714
Of course, Dad.

582
00:38:19,797 --> 00:38:22,008
And me, too, right?

583
00:38:22,091 --> 00:38:25,636
-Of course, Butchoy.
-[Ramon] Hold on.

584
00:38:25,720 --> 00:38:29,890
Why do we have two
lovely ladies with us today?

585
00:38:29,974 --> 00:38:32,601
Nimfa and Miss Ivy.

586
00:38:32,935 --> 00:38:33,894
Thank you.

587
00:38:34,562 --> 00:38:37,440
Miss Ivy is prettier, Mr. Ramon.

588
00:38:37,732 --> 00:38:40,901
Plus, she's rich and intelligent.

589
00:38:42,361 --> 00:38:44,196
You're beautiful, too, Nimfa.
But thank you.

590
00:38:46,032 --> 00:38:47,825
Mr. Mayor, you should be proud.

591
00:38:48,159 --> 00:38:50,703
The people of Ardiente
aren't just hardworking,

592
00:38:51,037 --> 00:38:52,163
they're good people.

593
00:38:52,830 --> 00:38:54,999
Ah… Mr. Fernan.

594
00:38:55,666 --> 00:38:57,626
That sounded so genuine.

595
00:38:57,835 --> 00:38:59,920
I just wish you were sincere about that.

596
00:39:02,757 --> 00:39:04,925
Come again, Miss Loring?

597
00:39:05,676 --> 00:39:07,094
It's so hot today.

598
00:39:07,178 --> 00:39:09,347
Gosh. Good thing it's breezy!

599
00:39:09,430 --> 00:39:12,683
[Loring and Nimfa chuckle]

600
00:39:17,813 --> 00:39:19,732
Lara, can I talk to Mom?

601
00:39:20,358 --> 00:39:21,942
Sorry, sir.

602
00:39:22,026 --> 00:39:23,861
You don't have an appointment
with the governor.

603
00:39:23,944 --> 00:39:27,531
Why don't you wait for her
to come home, instead?

604
00:39:27,740 --> 00:39:30,659
Lara, please. She needs to read this.

605
00:39:30,785 --> 00:39:34,413
If she doesn't, the farmers
might lose their livelihood.

606
00:39:35,373 --> 00:39:36,832
You understand that, right?

607
00:39:38,751 --> 00:39:39,794
Wait here, sir.

608
00:39:45,633 --> 00:39:48,719
I think Emilia still has time to catch up

609
00:39:48,803 --> 00:39:50,638
with Julio's popularity.

610
00:39:50,721 --> 00:39:52,306
Excuse me, Madam Governor.

611
00:39:52,390 --> 00:39:54,225
I'm really very sorry to interrupt,

612
00:39:54,308 --> 00:39:56,477
but someone's looking for you.

613
00:39:56,560 --> 00:39:59,021
-Who is it?
-It's Diego.

614
00:39:59,105 --> 00:40:01,399
Can you please tell him
I'm in the middle of a meeting?

615
00:40:01,482 --> 00:40:02,858
We'll just talk at home.

616
00:40:02,942 --> 00:40:04,735
-Yes, Madam.
-Let him in.

617
00:40:05,027 --> 00:40:09,532
Anyway, we're done here, Emilia.
We'll talk some other time.

618
00:40:11,367 --> 00:40:13,369
-Thank you, Senator Jose.
-You're welcome.

619
00:40:13,452 --> 00:40:14,662
Senator Magno.

620
00:40:21,043 --> 00:40:23,087
[tense music playing]

621
00:40:45,276 --> 00:40:46,485
Excuse us for a bit.

622
00:40:46,569 --> 00:40:48,737
We'll just get you something to drink.

623
00:40:48,821 --> 00:40:50,197
-[Nimfa] Oh.
-Thank you.

624
00:40:50,281 --> 00:40:51,240
-I'm coming with you.
-Let's go.

625
00:40:51,323 --> 00:40:52,533
Come on.

626
00:40:54,827 --> 00:40:56,036
-Miss Loring.
-Yes?

627
00:40:56,412 --> 00:40:57,246
[chuckles softly]

628
00:40:57,329 --> 00:41:00,791
I still have a chance with Diego, right?

629
00:41:01,083 --> 00:41:01,959
Of course.

630
00:41:02,042 --> 00:41:05,629
Don't worry about that.
Diego really doesn't like her.

631
00:41:05,713 --> 00:41:07,006
-[Nimfa] I knew it.
-[Loring] Yeah.

632
00:41:07,089 --> 00:41:08,799
[Loring] She doesn't like him, either.

633
00:41:09,467 --> 00:41:13,220
Wait. Do you think I'm his type?

634
00:41:13,304 --> 00:41:16,891
Did I say you weren't?
No, I didn't. I didn't say that.

635
00:41:16,974 --> 00:41:20,728
Forget about that. Don't worry.
You have a good chance.

636
00:41:20,811 --> 00:41:25,691
Let's just say that Miss Ivy
just has nice makeup on.

637
00:41:25,774 --> 00:41:29,945
-[both chuckling]
-I knew it!

638
00:41:30,029 --> 00:41:32,364
-Miss Loring, Nimfa.
-Yes?

639
00:41:33,782 --> 00:41:36,994
Can you tell me what's so funny?

640
00:41:38,579 --> 00:41:40,789
It's nothing, Ms. Ivy.

641
00:41:40,873 --> 00:41:45,252
Um. Why are you here, anyway?
You and the mayor.

642
00:41:45,336 --> 00:41:47,421
-[Arnaldo] Friends!
-Oh.

643
00:41:47,505 --> 00:41:51,008
Can you please come closer?
I'd like to say a few words.

644
00:41:51,467 --> 00:41:52,510
[Loring] Here we go.

645
00:41:54,970 --> 00:41:58,891
Well, we're here because…

646
00:41:59,517 --> 00:42:02,186
And I've said this before.

647
00:42:02,520 --> 00:42:05,689
We're planning to put up
an export processing zone

648
00:42:05,773 --> 00:42:08,776
here in Poblacion Ardiente.

649
00:42:09,318 --> 00:42:11,445
So, I'm here as your mayor,

650
00:42:11,529 --> 00:42:15,282
and Ivy's here as the
consultant for the project

651
00:42:15,366 --> 00:42:17,952
to ask for your support.

652
00:42:20,538 --> 00:42:22,373
You all need to vacate this property.

653
00:42:22,456 --> 00:42:23,916
-What?!
-What?

654
00:42:23,999 --> 00:42:27,044
[townsfolk murmuring indistinctly]

655
00:42:27,127 --> 00:42:28,671
You know, this is useless!

656
00:42:28,754 --> 00:42:30,464
We've already issued an eviction notice!

657
00:42:30,548 --> 00:42:32,007
Mom, hear them out first.

658
00:42:32,925 --> 00:42:36,720
The two of you have given me
nothing but problems.

659
00:42:36,804 --> 00:42:39,723
You always leave to see your mistress.

660
00:42:39,807 --> 00:42:42,101
And you. Why can't you wrap your head

661
00:42:42,184 --> 00:42:45,020
around the idea that we don't
owe anything to those farmers?

662
00:42:45,104 --> 00:42:46,730
You are an Ardiente,

663
00:42:46,814 --> 00:42:49,316
that's why you don't have
to side with them on this issue!

664
00:42:49,400 --> 00:42:51,569
No, Mom. If you'd only hear them out,

665
00:42:51,652 --> 00:42:53,862
you'd understand
what you're doing is wrong.

666
00:42:54,154 --> 00:42:55,155
Mayor…

667
00:42:56,156 --> 00:42:58,075
I don't think this is right.

668
00:42:59,702 --> 00:43:04,790
What about our livelihood?
We can't just leave this place.

669
00:43:05,332 --> 00:43:07,459
-She's right.
-We won't allow this.

670
00:43:07,543 --> 00:43:09,712
[crowd murmuring indistinctly]

671
00:43:09,795 --> 00:43:11,589
Mr. Pandoy, Miss Loring.

672
00:43:11,672 --> 00:43:13,173
Based on this document,

673
00:43:13,257 --> 00:43:16,719
we've given you a lot of time to move out.

674
00:43:16,802 --> 00:43:19,888
But don't worry.
We'll relocate you elsewhere.

675
00:43:20,264 --> 00:43:22,558
You just have to leave
as soon as possible.

676
00:43:22,641 --> 00:43:23,392
Hold on, sir.

677
00:43:23,475 --> 00:43:25,019
But you're not telling us
where you'll relocate us.

678
00:43:25,102 --> 00:43:26,937
We don't even know if we can start anew.

679
00:43:27,021 --> 00:43:31,358
Are you telling us to leave,
Mayor and Miss Beautiful?

680
00:43:31,900 --> 00:43:34,945
Please don't make us leave.

681
00:43:35,279 --> 00:43:37,823
We'll lose our homes again.

682
00:43:37,906 --> 00:43:40,242
We won't have anywhere to go.

683
00:43:41,952 --> 00:43:45,122
What else can't you understand?!

684
00:43:46,165 --> 00:43:48,542
You're wasting my time. Leave.

685
00:43:48,876 --> 00:43:49,877
-Mom.
-Leave!

686
00:43:49,960 --> 00:43:52,046
[tense music playing]

687
00:44:08,145 --> 00:44:09,063
[gasps]

688
00:44:10,230 --> 00:44:11,190
[groans]

689
00:44:11,940 --> 00:44:13,025
[grunts]

690
00:44:15,486 --> 00:44:19,073
[tense music playing]

691
00:44:36,006 --> 00:44:38,008
-[Arnaldo] <i>Careful.</i>
-[people exclaim]

692
00:44:38,092 --> 00:44:39,426
[Arnaldo] <i>I didn't like</i>
<i>what you did earlier.</i>

693
00:44:39,510 --> 00:44:41,512
[Diego] <i>If you always got</i>
<i>what you wanted back then,</i>

694
00:44:41,595 --> 00:44:43,472
<i>it won't happen this time.</i>
<i>Ivy doesn't like you.</i>

695
00:44:43,555 --> 00:44:45,641
[Ivy] <i>You've been best friends</i>
<i>since you were kids?</i>

696
00:44:45,724 --> 00:44:48,143
[Loring] <i>Diego had only one best friend.</i>

697
00:44:48,227 --> 00:44:51,772
<i>And she was his one and only true love.</i>

698
00:44:51,855 --> 00:44:53,690
<i>Her name is Lily.</i>

699
00:44:53,774 --> 00:44:56,860
<i>I have here an old draft,</i>
<i>the deed of donation</i>

700
00:44:56,944 --> 00:44:59,947
<i>confirming that the land</i>
<i>was donated to the farmers.</i>

701
00:45:00,030 --> 00:45:01,031
[Arnaldo] <i>You're different.</i>

702
00:45:01,115 --> 00:45:05,536
<i>Perfect characteristics</i>
<i>of a first lady. My first lady.</i>

703
00:45:05,619 --> 00:45:06,870
[Diego] <i>Miss Aguas, wait.</i>

704
00:45:08,539 --> 00:45:11,333
[theme music playing]
